WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:03.240
Is "Halloween Ends" really the end?

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.580
And why does its star think the film will
make fans "very angry"?

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:09.870
Here's all you need to know before the big
premiere.

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:16.947
The official release date for "Halloween Ends"
is October 14, 2022, just in time for the holiday.

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:22.685
Filming for "Halloween Ends" initially began
in January 2022 and concluded a few months later in March.

00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:27.899
Pre-pandemic, Blumhouse Studios had planned
to release "Halloween Kills" in October 2020,

00:00:27.899 --> 00:00:30.460
and "Halloween Ends" one year later in 2021.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.340
Of course, delays due to COVID-19 threw a
wrench into production, so the pair of sequels

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:36.960
were pushed back by a year.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.467
Studios generally like to release "Halloween"
films, well, around Halloween — which seems like a no-brainer.

00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:43.629
"You know it's Halloween.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:46.690
Everyone's entitled to one good scare, huh?"

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:51.420
This was the case for the first five original
"Halloween" films, which all debuted theatrically

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:52.750
in the month of October.

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:57.550
The sixth just barely squeaked in with a September
29 release date.

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:02.719
This trend was surprisingly dropped in favor
of summer releases for "Halloween: H20" and

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:06.290
"Halloween: Resurrection," as well as Rob
Zombie's duo of reboots.

00:01:06.290 --> 00:01:10.490
However, with the appearance of David Gordon
Green's new trilogy, "Halloween" has returned

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:15.229
to its classic fall schedule, with "Halloween
Ends" wrapping up the tradition by releasing

00:01:15.229 --> 00:01:17.630
around the same time of year as its predecessors.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:24.440
The 2018 "Halloween" film brought Jamie Lee
Curtis back to the iconic role of Laurie Strode,

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:29.870
and introduced two new generations in Laurie's
daughter Karen (played by Judy Greer) and

00:01:29.870 --> 00:01:32.900
her granddaughter Allyson (played Andi Matichak).

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.500
Though this central trio survived that film
and made it to the climax of the follow-up,

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:43.916
"Halloween Kills" ended on a shocking note
as Michael murdered Karen just before the credits started.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:45.409
"So many people are dead!

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:46.700
We're not equipped!"

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.890
Curtis and Matichak are back one last time
in "Halloween Ends," with James Jude Courtney

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:56.680
and original actor Nick Castle joining forces
to bring Michael Myers to life, as they did

00:01:56.680 --> 00:01:58.250
on the two previous entries.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:03.450
Kyle Richards is also back once again as Lindsay
Wallace, Laurie's 1978 babysitting charge

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:07.729
who managed to again narrowly escape Michael's
knife in "Halloween Kills."

00:02:07.729 --> 00:02:12.730
Trilogy mainstays Will Patton and Omar Dorsey
round out the returning cast members.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:17.220
Joining the cast is former "Guiding Light"
star Michael O'Leary as Dr. Mathis, a character

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:20.070
mentioned but not seen in "Halloween Kills."

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:24.630
Rohan Campbell of Hulu's "The Hardy Boys"
will also provide a fresh face as a new character

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:25.800
named Corey Cunningham.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:31.400
The official synopsis for "Halloween Ends"
explains that, rather than picking up exactly

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.220
where we left off in "Halloween Kills," the
story will resume four years later.

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:41.128
Laurie Strode and her granddaughter Allyson
are living together, and there's no Michael Myers in sight.

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:45.350
We can assume that the movie will have Laurie
and Michael locked in a final showdown of

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:49.320
sorts — at least, a final showdown for this
iteration of the franchise.

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:52.660
As for the fate of these two characters, who
can say for certain?

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:57.120
In an interview with Total Film Magazine,
Jamie Lee Curtis, producer Malek Akkad, and

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.910
director David Gordon Green gave a few hints
as to what audiences might expect from the

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:03.650
final film in the trilogy.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:07.370
After "Halloween Kills" focused on the town
of Haddonfield at large, it seems like we're

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:12.100
in for a shift, with Akkad revealing that
the final film in the trilogy will be, in

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.900
his words, "way more contained."

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:16.360
"What the hell is happening?"

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:16.977
"It's Michael.

00:03:16.977 --> 00:03:17.977
It's gotta be."

00:03:17.977 --> 00:03:22.391
As for Green, he went on to elaborate slightly,
suggesting that the final "Halloween" film

00:03:22.391 --> 00:03:27.370
— which was originally planned to take place
on the same 2018 Halloween night as both its

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:30.870
predecessors — may be something fans won't
expect.

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:31.870
He told Total Film,

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.090
"I get engaged by doing something different.

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.760
If I was just going to be repetitive, I would
hand the reins off to someone else.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:42.840
When you have that opportunity within an established
franchise, it's really fun to think about

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:46.170
how you can show different tones and perspectives
and evolve."

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:53.160
The iconic not-so-sleepy town of Haddonfield,
Illinois, is one of the most infamous movie

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.060
towns in horror history, and also one of the
deadliest.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:01.770
While the original John Carpenter film was
shot in Los Angeles County, the most recent

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:04.890
"Halloween" trilogy traveled to the opposite
coast to film.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.960
The 2018 "Halloween" was mostly filmed in
the low country of South Carolina.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:13.070
The second installment, "Halloween Kills,"
was filmed mostly in North Carolina.

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:18.079
Interestingly, "Halloween Ends" was shot primarily
in and around the Savannah, Georgia area,

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:19.889
though not exclusively.

00:04:19.889 --> 00:04:24.259
According to the film's IMDb page, photography
for "Ends" also took place in part around

00:04:24.259 --> 00:04:30.460
Salt Lake City, Utah, a vast departure from
the east coast locations and the film's midwestern

00:04:30.460 --> 00:04:34.900
setting, leaving fans wondering just where
the final installment might take us.

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:39.949
The new "Halloween" trilogy, beginning with
the 2018 film, is largely the brainchild of

00:04:39.949 --> 00:04:44.849
filmmakers and longtime collaborators David
Gordon Green and Danny McBride.

00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:49.509
Though Green and McBride were both new to
the horror genre, they were longtime fans

00:04:49.509 --> 00:04:55.430
of John Carpenter and Debra Hill's original
1978 "Halloween," and opted to ignore all

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.770
previous sequels and remakes.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:00.930
Green went on to direct all three films in
this new trilogy.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:04.919
Evidently, even though they ignored all the
previous installments in the franchise, it

00:05:04.919 --> 00:05:10.540
still reportedly took Green and McBride more
than 80 drafts of the screenplay to "get it

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:15.639
right," with rewrites happening as late as
one week before production, according to

00:05:15.639 --> 00:05:16.639
The Hollywood Reporter.

00:05:16.639 --> 00:05:22.080
"Michael Myers, loose, with a bunch of nutbags
in Haddonfield on Halloween night?!"

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:27.099
The duo of Green and McBride returned to write
the screenplay for "Halloween Kills" alongside

00:05:27.099 --> 00:05:32.909
Scott Teems, resulting in a sequel that proved
more polarizing than its crowd-pleasing predecessor.

00:05:32.909 --> 00:05:37.389
Green and McBride also co-wrote the screenplay
for "Halloween Ends," this time alongside

00:05:37.389 --> 00:05:39.590
Paul Brad Logan and Chris Bernier.

00:05:40.689 --> 00:05:43.430
When 2018's "Halloween" was released, it was
a simpler time.

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:47.889
The film arrived in theaters and then quickly
made its way to home video soon after, with

00:05:47.889 --> 00:05:52.800
the second and third films in David Gordon
Green's planned trilogy being greenlit almost

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.800
immediately following its success.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.009
Unfortunately, it would be another three years
before "Halloween Kills" would be released

00:05:59.009 --> 00:06:05.690
due to the COVID-19 pandemic, with the sequel's
initial release of October 2020 being shifted to October 2021.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.200
"Halloween Ends" began filming not long after
the release of "Halloween Kills," with a set

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.770
release date for October 2022.

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:17.460
With only a year between these two films,
Green's two sequels will follow an '80s slasher

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:20.760
movie tradition of immediate back-to-back
entries.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:24.749
The earlier "Halloween" series even sporadically
followed this pattern for a while — "Halloween

00:06:24.749 --> 00:06:30.340
II" was released in October 1981, continuing
the story from the first film, with the largely

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:34.123
unrelated "Halloween III: Season of the Witch"
coming out a year later.

00:06:38.800 --> 00:06:43.629
In October 1988, "Halloween 4: The Return
of Michael Myers" was released, which brought

00:06:43.629 --> 00:06:48.130
Myers back from his comatose state, leading
into "Halloween 5: The Revenge of Michael

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:49.550
Myers" the following October.

00:06:49.550 --> 00:06:55.509
"Halloween Ends" is set to arrive in theaters
on October 14, 2022 and — as with "Halloween

00:06:55.509 --> 00:07:01.275
Kills" before it — will also be made available
on Peacock for the first 60 days of the film's release.

00:07:02.564 --> 00:07:07.960
The "Halloween" franchise is a bit complicated,
but most long-running horror series are.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:11.770
Including "Halloween Ends," there are 13 total
films in the saga, though not all of them

00:07:11.770 --> 00:07:14.960
are necessary to enjoy this final trilogy
installment.

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:20.330
The only movie in the anthology that every
other film tends to stem from is the original

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:26.740
1978 "Halloween," which introduced the world
to both Michael Myers and Laurie Strode.

00:07:26.740 --> 00:07:31.809
This masterpiece has become an icon over the
past four decades, and no matter how many

00:07:31.809 --> 00:07:37.596
new "Halloween" sequels or reboots hit the
screen, none can escape the shadow of the original.

00:07:37.620 --> 00:07:41.930
The original "Halloween II," "Halloween 4:
The Return of Michael Myers," "Halloween 5:

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:46.539
The Revenge of Michael Myers," and "Halloween:
The Curse of Michael Myers" all follow in

00:07:46.539 --> 00:07:48.430
the timeline begun with the original.

00:07:48.430 --> 00:07:52.830
The third installment, "Halloween III: Season
of the Witch," has nothing to do with the

00:07:52.830 --> 00:07:59.147
overall continuity, beyond the original movie
playing on TV within its story about killer Halloween masks.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:05.080
Then, in 1998, "Halloween H20: 20 Years Later"
was released to commemorate the anniversary

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:10.479
of the original "Halloween," thus ignoring
all the sequels except "Halloween II."

00:08:10.479 --> 00:08:14.720
This film would spawn a sequel of its own
— "Halloween Resurrection" — which would

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:19.280
soon be ignored by Rob Zombie's two "Halloween"
reboot films beginning in 2007.

00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:22.511
"Michael, you know I'm not really here."

00:08:22.511 --> 00:08:28.389
"Halloween Ends" fits in a timeline composed
of the original 1978 film, the 2018 "Halloween,"

00:08:28.389 --> 00:08:29.520
and "Halloween Kills."

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:34.760
This effectively sets aside all the convoluted
sequel plot threads concerning secret familial

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:40.720
relationships and ancient cults, instead focusing
in on the pure slasher element of an unknowable

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.259
killer and his tenacious prey.

00:08:43.970 --> 00:08:48.210
There's no doubt that David Gordon Green's
take on the "Halloween" mythos isn't for everybody.

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:52.660
Removing the brother-sister connection between
Michael Myers and Laurie Strode was a gutsy

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:58.927
move, especially given that the vast majority
of the franchise has kept that part of their story intact.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:03.420
This makes sense, given that John Carpenter
himself made them siblings while working on

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.680
"Halloween II" and the expanded TV broadcast
of the original film.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:10.020
Carpenter admitted to ComicBook.com in 2019,

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:12.000
"I came up with this brother thing.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.040
It was awful, just awful.

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.220
But I did it."

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:20.010
Nevertheless, the 2018 "Halloween" revival
disregarded this plotline completely, with

00:09:20.010 --> 00:09:24.950
Carpenter's blessing, opting to start anew
with only the original 1978 film remaining

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:26.310
a part of the story.

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:30.870
This alone was frustrating for some fans,
though for others it was a new beginning,

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:35.130
and one that sparked new life in an otherwise
aimless franchise.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:40.180
According to series star Jamie Lee Curtis,
many fans might not love "Halloween Ends,"

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.460
the final installment in this rebooted trilogy
of slashers.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:44.460
She told NME,

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:49.340
"It's going to make people very angry, and
it's going to be shocking because it asks

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:50.510
a lot of questions.

00:09:50.510 --> 00:09:52.620
So that's all I can tell you."

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:57.630
Wherever the conclusion to this modern "Halloween"
trilogy takes us, it seems it will be somewhere

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.540
we've never gone before.

00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:05.200
This might be scary to some longtime Michael
Myers fans, but the possibility of an unprecedented

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:12.586
and surprising conclusion may be just the
kind of uncertainty the "Halloween" franchise needs.

00:10:12.610 --> 00:10:17.560
For more than 40 years, Jamie Lee Curtis has
come and gone from her role as the iconic

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:22.280
"final girl" Laurie Strode, continuously escaping
the clutches of Michael Myers.

00:10:22.280 --> 00:10:26.615
Now, "Halloween Ends" promises, well, an end
to all that.

00:10:26.615 --> 00:10:28.720
"Evil dies tonight!"

00:10:28.720 --> 00:10:33.440
This means that either Laurie is set to die
in combat against Michael, or live happily

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.820
ever after once he's six feet under.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:41.380
Whichever ending befalls our horror heroine,
it will surely be thrilling to see her story

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:43.690
get a definitive conclusion here.

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:48.550
Jamie Lee Curtis has implied in a video promoting
"Halloween Ends" that this is her last time

00:10:48.550 --> 00:10:49.840
playing Laurie Strode.

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:51.490
She went on to explain to Total Film,

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:54.200
"I'm not saying something like, 'Oh, because
I die!'

00:10:54.200 --> 00:10:55.270
It's nothing to do with that.

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:58.260
I'm talking about emotionally what they have
constructed.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.776
I think it will be a spectacular way to end
this trilogy."

00:11:02.480 --> 00:11:07.440
With a title like "Halloween Ends," there
are some pretty serious implications attached.

00:11:07.440 --> 00:11:11.830
No doubt, this is the end to David Gordon
Green's sequel trilogy of "Halloween" films,

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:16.120
meant to be a love-letter of sorts to the
original John Carpenter classic.

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:20.760
With Jamie Lee Curtis evidently satisfied
with the film's conclusion and the plot seemingly

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:25.330
wrapped up here, it sounds like "Halloween
Ends" might actually be the final chapter

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.730
of the "Halloween" saga.

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:30.240
And what better film to end on than the 13th!

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:35.000
Of course, John Carpenter has his own thoughts
on the continuation of the "Halloween" brand.

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.370
Carpenter told ComicBook.com,

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:40.570
"If you take a dollar sign and attach it to
anything ... it will live.

00:11:40.570 --> 00:11:45.440
If the dollar sign is not big enough, no matter
what, it will not live.

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:47.310
This time, I do not know.

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:49.060
They really want to end.

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.180
They're going to shut it off, end it.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:52.920
It's what David has in mind.

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:53.920
That's fine."

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.200
In an interview with ScreenRant, producer
Jason Blum went on record and reminded us

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:02.970
that this is Blumhouse Productions' last "Halloween"
movie, and while that doesn't necessarily

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:07.490
mean that Michael Myers won't return someday,
their work on the franchise is complete.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:08.490
Blum said,

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:12.060
"This is our last one and I think people will
be very happy."

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:16.510
So it looks like "Halloween Ends" is the culmination
of the franchise as we know it currently,

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:19.896
but that doesn't mean it's the end for "Halloween"
as a whole.

